{
  "per_column": [
    {"name": "incident_category", "analytical_usefulness": 0.95, "source_groundedness": 0.95, "hallucination_observed": false, "rationale": "Essential for isolating hardware incidents, the base denominator of the query. Values align well with short_description (installation->software, MySQL->database)."},
    {"name": "failure_mode", "analytical_usefulness": 1.0, "source_groundedness": 0.9, "hallucination_observed": false, "rationale": "Directly answers 'most common failure causes' — the core of the query. NULLs for non-hardware/silent rows are appropriate. Connectivity_failure from MySQL text is well grounded."},
    {"name": "recurrence_signal", "analytical_usefulness": 0.55, "source_groundedness": 0.5, "hallucination_observed": true, "rationale": "Recurrence could inform which causes drive incident rate, but a boolean flag derived from a single short_description is weakly grounded; the source text gives little basis to assert repeat occurrence per row."},
    {"name": "affected_scope", "analytical_usefulness": 0.6, "source_groundedness": 0.5, "hallucination_observed": true, "rationale": "Scope adds a plausible grouping axis, but values like 'individual_device' for a bare 'software installation' text are confident specifics the source does not clearly support; MySQL->production_system is more defensible."},
    {"name": "software_issue_subtype", "analytical_usefulness": 0.3, "source_groundedness": 0.9, "hallucination_observed": false, "rationale": "Well grounded (installation, update_failure, database_connectivity map cleanly to text) but pertains to software incidents, offering little leverage for a query specifically about hardware failure causes."}
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.7,
  "source_groundedness": 0.75,
  "rationale": "incident_category and failure_mode together directly enable the query: they let the analyst isolate hardware incidents, rank failure causes, and estimate the rate reduction from addressing the top ones — high usefulness and solid grounding. affected_scope and recurrence_signal add secondary axes but assert per-row specifics (device scope, recurrence) that the terse short_descriptions do not clearly warrant, lowering groundedness. software_issue_subtype is well grounded but tangential to a hardware-focused query. Overall a useful, mostly grounded set with some unsupported confident values."
}

